 ## Overview
-GRay Optimization Settings define the hyperparameter configurations for training 3D Gaussian Splatting using the GRay ray-tracing renderer [S1]. Unlike standard 3DGS and 3DGRT, GRay does not use opacity resets and does not prune Gaussians based on size [S1]. The settings control the trade-off between training speed, final frame rate, and reconstruction quality through alpha thresholds, pruning thresholds, and spherical harmonic stepping laziness.
+GRay Optimization Settings define the hyperparameter configurations for training the GRay ray-tracing renderer, which differs from standard 3D Gaussian Splatting (3DGS) by omitting opacity resets and size-based pruning [S1]. It provides two distinct presets: GRayLQ for high-speed, low-quality training and GRayHQ for high-quality reconstruction, allowing users to balance initialization time, optimization duration, and final rendering fidelity [S1].
 
